The hard grind is on at Swift and Hulse's alleys. There are twelve teams in the race and already a few have dropped back several steps. The Gel erys who took the lead at the start have maintained it but the Pumpkins, Potatoes, Tomatoes and Parsnips are most daily sending a thrill of fear through the bodies of the five men team leaders.

 At the close of last week the Pump kins, Potatoes and Tomatoes were but one lap behind and it Is unnecessary to state that they will endeavor to root out the Celerys. The Cabbages who tumbled at the start are fighting 1t out half way down the line and seem satis- fled to maintain their present hold in the race. A short distance behind the Onions are working hard to continue as leaders of the second division. The Car rots and Turnips are pushing ahead neck to neck, each endeavoring to get a permanent grasp on the eighth sta- tion of the grand circuit. A lap behind these formidable opponents which Is the Sduashes and Radishes, confident of some day making their way to the top of the list. but at present have two team fight for tenth place. The Red Peppers. forgotten by their ambitious contemporaries are slowly lingering and limping about the track. pitifully glancing from one side to the other hoping to see friendly face or some one who will comfort them in their dis tress.

 welch Is the honor man In the grand twelve team race while Moeller and Miller follow short distance in tho rear. H. Raush still holds Gates under submission at the bottom of the heap. The records follow;

article_spellcheck:
The hard grind is on at Swift and Hulse's alleys. There are twelve teams in the race and already a few have dropped back several steps. The Celerys who took the lead at the start have maintained it but the Pumpkins, Potatoes, Tomatoes and Parsnips are most daily sending a thrill of fear through the bodies of the five men team leaders.

At the close of last week the Pumpkins, Potatoes and Tomatoes were but one lap behind and it is unnecessary to state that they will endeavor to root out the Celerys. The Cabbages who tumbled at the start are fighting it out half way down the line and seem satisfied to maintain their present hold in the race. A short distance behind the Onions are working hard to continue as leaders of the second division. The Carrots and Turnips are pushing ahead neck to neck, each endeavoring to get a permanent grasp on the eighth station of the grand circuit. A lap behind these formidable opponents which is the Squashes and Radishes, confident of some day making their way to the top of the list, but at present have two team fight for tenth place. The Red Peppers, forgotten by their ambitious contemporaries, are slowly lingering and limping about the track, pitifully glancing from one side to the other hoping to see friendly face or some one who will comfort them in their distress.

Welch is the honor man in the grand twelve team race while Moeller and Miller follow short distance in the rear. H. Raush still holds Gates under submission at the bottom of the heap. The records follow;

